# Deploy a Worker

This is a preview with a qualified compiler and an explicit managed capability
profile. Hosted JSPI, disposable hosted SQLite/live acceptance and local conformance
are measured separately from release publication. Start with the unchanged one-file
counter, which uses ordinary typed SQLite and finite Datastar fragments.

```sh
rocci worker init examples/rocci/standalone/counter --provider cloudflare
cd examples/rocci/standalone/counter
npm install
npm run dev
```

Init preserves `Counter.rocci`. Review `rocci.toml`: all visitors share the
explicit object key, and `./counter.db` maps to that object's managed database.
The generated `wrangler.jsonc` supplies one stable SQLite class migration and
a custom build hook. Keep those identities when rebuilding/deploying. Secrets,
accounts, routes and authentication use ordinary Wrangler configuration.

Build automatically resolves the pinned compiler and host archive. Automatic
installation supports Apple Silicon macOS and x64 Linux. During development of
this unreleased implementation, maintainers must supply its built archive;
prebuilt download requires the corresponding release. No Rust or C compiler
is needed when using the released CLI/host package. Generated files live in
`.rocci/worker/`; commit authored configuration, npm locks and
`rocci-worker.lock`, and keep generated outputs ignored.

```sh
rocci worker build --locked
npx wrangler login
npm run deploy
```

Deployment is an explicit provider operation that may create billable managed
resources. Choose authentication and public routes for your application before
publishing it. Direct `wrangler dev` and `wrangler deploy` run the same hook.
For an unrelated page without SQL, start with
`rocci worker init my-page --stateless`. Plain Roc programs can use the same
platform without templates; examples live in `rocci-worker-platform/examples`.

Read [configuration](/docs/reference/configuration/),
[runtime limits](/docs/reference/runtime/) and
[troubleshooting](/docs/troubleshooting/runtime/) before relying on a native
effect. Native filesystem/process/socket behavior and shutdown guarantees do
not transfer to Workers. Durable state stays in SQL, and live browser state
stays server rendered.

The scaffold watches existing root source files and authored directories,
including an assets directory. Add newly created root source files to
Wrangler `build.watch_dir` or restart after a manual build; files inside
watched directories are discovered automatically. Keep generated directories
and provider logs outside that watch list.

The lock retains compiler fingerprints per development host, so macOS and
Linux builds do not overwrite each other. Review one unlocked build on each
new host architecture before requiring `--locked` there. The compiler pin,
Wasm host and runtime remain common to the application.
